WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Heat pumps are the future of residential HVAC. R-410A replacements are all heat
pump compatible.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Ductwork design determines system performance. Supply ducts carry conditioned
air to rooms. Return ducts bring air back. Total external static pressure (TESP)
measures the resistance the blower must overcome. Maximum TESP for most

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
TESP: Total External Static Pressure. Sum of supply and return static. Maximum
0.50 in w.c. for most residential.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
CFM: Cubic Feet per Minute. Airflow volume. Typical residential is 400 CFM per
ton of cooling.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Many comfort complaints are duct problems
not equipment problems. Measuring static pressure identifies duct issues.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: 0.50 in w.c. maximum TESP. And — 400 CFM per ton is the
standard airflow target

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

